From: cyy <cyyever@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ws2_32: WSALookupServiceBegin semi-stub succeeds with an empty set

WSALookupServiceBegin{A,W} are unimplemented stubs that hard-fail with
WSA_NOT_ENOUGH_MEMORY (error 8). Steam's CEF webhelper (Chromium) drives its
network_change_notifier through WSALookupServiceBeginW to enumerate networks;
the perpetual failure spams "WSALookupServiceBegin failed with: 8" in cef_log
and contributes to the network service stalling during init.

Return success with an empty result set instead: Begin hands back a sentinel
handle, Next reports WSA_E_NO_MORE (already correct), End succeeds. The
notifier then sees "no networks / no changes" and finishes that step. Real
NLA/service discovery remains unimplemented — callers simply see no services,
which is strictly better than the hard failure they got before. (Upstream Wine
gap, not Proton-specific; proper fix belongs in WineHQ.)

---
diff --git a/dlls/ws2_32/protocol.c b/dlls/ws2_32/protocol.c
--- a/dlls/ws2_32/protocol.c
+++ b/dlls/ws2_32/protocol.c
@@ -2217,9 +2217,9 @@
  */
 int WINAPI WSALookupServiceBeginA( WSAQUERYSETA *query, DWORD flags, HANDLE *lookup )
 {
-    FIXME( "(%p %#lx %p) Stub!\n", query, flags, lookup );
-    SetLastError( WSA_NOT_ENOUGH_MEMORY );
-    return -1;
+    FIXME( "(%p %#lx %p) semi-stub: returning empty result set\n", query, flags, lookup );
+    *lookup = (HANDLE)(ULONG_PTR)1;
+    return 0;
 }


@@ -2228,9 +2228,9 @@
  */
 int WINAPI WSALookupServiceBeginW( WSAQUERYSETW *query, DWORD flags, HANDLE *lookup )
 {
-    FIXME( "(%p %#lx %p) Stub!\n", query, flags, lookup );
-    SetLastError( WSA_NOT_ENOUGH_MEMORY );
-    return -1;
+    FIXME( "(%p %#lx %p) semi-stub: returning empty result set\n", query, flags, lookup );
+    *lookup = (HANDLE)(ULONG_PTR)1;
+    return 0;
 }
